// Per-variant visibility is rejected by design, not merely unimplemented.
//
// Work it through: with `private B` in module M and a `match` in module N, either
// exhaustiveness demands N name `B` — which N is forbidden to write, a
// contradiction — or it exempts private variants, and then the only total form
// needs a `_` arm. A non-exhaustive match in Saffron yields an indeterminate
// value rather than an error (BUGS #76), so that second reading makes the safe
// form unwritable and the unsafe form silently wrong. A feature whose only
// expressible use is a footgun is not a feature.
//
// `private enum Mode` — the whole type — IS supported and has none of this
// interaction: a module that cannot name the type cannot match on it at all.
// test/pass/visibility_parse.sf covers that form.
enum Mode {
    private On,
    Off
}

var m: Mode = Mode.Off
IO.println("built")
